

--> JWT Security
    JWT is a stateless authentication mechanism used mainly in REST APIs.
    Once a token is issued, the server does not store user session data

--> JWT Flow
    Step-by-Step Flow
        Client sends username & password to /login
        Server validates credentials
        Server generates JWT token
        Token is returned to client
        Client sends token in
        Authorization: Bearer <token>
        Server validates token on every request
        Access granted if token is valid
        No session, no server-side storage

--> Securing REST APIs with JWT – Theory
        ✔ JWT works with filters, not sessions
        ✔ Every request passes through JWT filter
        ✔ Token validated before controller execution
        ✔ Stateless → High scalability

